package views

import (
	"github.com/Francesco99975/shorehamex2/internal/config"
	"github.com/Francesco99975/shorehamex2/views/layouts"
)

templ PrivacyPolicy(site config.Site) {
	@layouts.Base(site) {
		<main
			class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center w-full p-2 text-primary text-center legal"
		>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p>Last updated: November 11, 2026</p>
			<p>This Privacy Policy describes how Casa Medica collects, uses, discloses and protects personal information, including personal health information, when it is handled through Casa Medica Examinations. It also tells You about Your privacy rights and how the law protects You.</p>
			<p>Casa Medica is the &quot;health information custodian&quot; responsible for Your information under Ontario's Personal Health Information Protection Act, 2004 (&quot;PHIPA&quot;). We collect, use and disclose Your information only as described in this Privacy Policy, with Your consent (express or implied), or as otherwise permitted or required by PHIPA and other applicable law.</p>
			<h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
			<h3>Interpretation</h3>
			<p>The words whose initial letters are capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. The following definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or in plural.</p>
			<h3>Definitions</h3>
			<p>For the purposes of this Privacy Policy:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Account</strong> means a unique account created for a Clinician to access the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Clinician</strong> means an authorized healthcare professional or staff member of Casa Medica who uses the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Company</strong> (referred to as either &quot;the Company&quot;, &quot;Casa Medica&quot;, &quot;We&quot;, &quot;Us&quot; or &quot;Our&quot; in this Privacy Policy) refers to Casa Medica, 140 Woodbridge Ave. Unit 17 Second Floor L4L 4K9.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Cookies</strong> are small files that are placed on Your computer, mobile device or any other device by a website.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Country/State</strong> refers to: Ontario, Canada.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Device</strong> means any device that can access the Service, such as a computer, a cell phone or a digital tablet.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Examination</strong> means a test, questionnaire or assessment administered to a Patient through the Service, either remotely through an Examination Link or in person at the clinic.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Examination Link</strong> means a unique link sent by email to a Patient that gives access to a specific Examination.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Patient</strong> means an individual whose information is entered into the Service by a Clinician and who takes, or is asked to take, an Examination.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Personal Data</strong> (or &quot;Personal Information&quot;) is any information that relates to an identified or identifiable individual. It includes &quot;personal health information&quot; as defined in PHIPA.</p>
					<p>We use &quot;Personal Data&quot; and &quot;Personal Information&quot; interchangeably unless a law uses a specific term.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Service</strong> refers to Casa Medica Examinations, the Website and the tools it provides.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Service Provider</strong> means any natural or legal person who provides technical services to Us in order to operate the Service, such as software maintenance and server hosting, and who handles Personal Data only on Our behalf and under Our instructions.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Usage Data</strong> refers to data collected automatically, either generated by the use of the Service or from the Service infrastructure itself (for example, the time and date of a page visit).</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>User</strong> means any individual who accesses or uses the Service, including Clinicians and Patients.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Website</strong> refers to Casa Medica Examinations, accessible from <a href="https://casaintake.urx.ink" target="_blank">casaintake.urx.ink</a>.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing or using the Service, as applicable.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>Collecting and Using Your Personal Information</h2>
			<h3>Types of Data Collected</h3>
			<h4>Personal Data</h4>
			<p>Casa Medica Examinations is used by Clinicians to administer Examinations to Patients. Personal Data is entered into the Service by Clinicians, and by Patients when they complete an Examination. It includes:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>First name and last name</li>
				<li>Email address</li>
				<li>Phone number</li>
				<li>Date of birth</li>
				<li>Sex</li>
				<li>Examination responses, scores and results</li>
			</ul>
			<p>Clinicians' Account information (such as name, email address and login credentials) is also collected so that access to the Service can be limited to authorized staff.</p>
			<h4>Usage Data</h4>
			<p>Usage Data is collected automatically when using the Service.</p>
			<p>Usage Data may include information such as Your Device's Internet Protocol address (e.g. IP address), browser type, browser version, the pages of Our Service that You visit, and the time and date of Your visit.</p>
			<p>The Service also keeps audit records of who viewed, created or changed Patient information and when. These records help Us protect Your information and detect unauthorized access.</p>
			<h4>Cookies</h4>
			<p>We use only the Cookies that are strictly necessary to operate the Service securely. We do not use advertising, analytics or third-party tracking Cookies or web beacons on the Service. You can instruct Your browser to refuse all Cookies, but if You do, You may not be able to use the Service.</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Necessary / Essential Cookies</strong></p>
					<p>Type: Session Cookies</p>
					<p>Administered by: Us</p>
					<p>Purpose: These Cookies are essential to keep Clinicians signed in, to authenticate Users, to maintain the secure session of an Examination and to prevent fraudulent or unauthorized use of the Service. Without these Cookies, the Service cannot be provided.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<h3>Use of Your Personal Data</h3>
			<p>Casa Medica uses Personal Data for the following purposes:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To provide healthcare and administer Examinations</strong>, including to record Examination responses and results so they can be reviewed by Your Clinician.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To manage Patient records:</strong> to create, maintain and update Patient records in connection with Your care.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To contact You:</strong> to send You an Examination Link by email, or to contact You by email or telephone about Your care, appointments or Examinations.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To manage Accounts:</strong> to manage Clinician access to the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To maintain and secure the Service:</strong> to keep the Service running, to detect and prevent unauthorized access, and to investigate security incidents.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>To meet legal and professional obligations:</strong> including record-keeping, responding to Your access and correction requests, and complying with the law.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<p>We do not sell Your Personal Data, and We do not use it for marketing or advertising.</p>
			<p>We may share Your Personal Data in the following situations:</p>
			<ul>
				<li><strong>Within Your circle of care:</strong> with Clinicians and staff at Casa Medica who need the information to provide or support Your care.</li>
				<li><strong>With Service Providers:</strong> Our Service Providers (including the software developer who maintains the Service and the company that hosts its servers) may technically have access to data stored in the Service. They may use it only as needed to provide their services to Us and may not disclose it. They are bound by written agreements requiring them to protect it.</li>
				<li><strong>With other healthcare providers:</strong> where You consent, or where PHIPA otherwise permits or requires it.</li>
				<li><strong>With Your consent</strong>: We may disclose Your Personal Data for any other purpose with Your consent.</li>
			</ul>
			<h4>Email Communications</h4>
			<p>When a Clinician sends You an Examination Link, We send an email to the address on Your record. This email contains the link and basic instructions only. It does not include Your test results or other health information. Examination Links are unique to You and may expire after a period of time or after use. Please do not forward or share Your Examination Link.</p>
			<p>Email is not a fully secure form of communication. If You do not wish to receive Examination Links by email, please tell Your Clinician, and You can take the Examination in person at the clinic instead.</p>
			<h3>Retention of Your Personal Data</h3>
			<p>Casa Medica retains Personal Data only for as long as necessary to provide care, to meet the record retention requirements that apply to health records under Ontario law and professional standards, and to meet Our other legal obligations.</p>
			<p>Patient records, including Examination responses and results, are retained for the period required for health records, and are then securely destroyed or de-identified. Clinician Account information is retained while the Clinician has access to the Service and for a reasonable period afterwards. Usage Data and audit records are retained for as long as needed for security, auditing and legal compliance.</p>
			<p>When retention periods expire, We securely delete or de-identify Personal Data. Residual copies may remain in encrypted backups for a limited period, and are not restored except where necessary for security, disaster recovery or legal compliance.</p>
			<p>You may request information about how long We will retain Your Personal Data by contacting Us.</p>
			<h3>Where Your Data Is Stored</h3>
			<p>Your information is stored on servers operated by a third-party hosting provider. Those servers may be located outside of Ontario and Canada, where data protection laws may differ from those of Ontario. We take steps to protect Your information wherever it is stored, including through encryption and access controls, and by requiring Our Service Providers to protect it and to use it only to provide services to Us.</p>
			<h3>Your Rights: Access, Correction and Deletion</h3>
			<p>Under PHIPA, You have the right to request access to Your personal health information held by Casa Medica, and to request that it be corrected if it is inaccurate or incomplete. You may also withdraw Your consent in certain circumstances, and You may ask about how Your information is handled.</p>
			<p>To make a request, contact Us using the details below. Please note that health records are subject to legal retention requirements, so We may not be able to delete certain information on request, and We will explain why where that is the case.</p>
			<h3>Disclosure of Your Personal Data</h3>
			<h4>Business Transactions</h4>
			<p>If Casa Medica changes ownership, closes or transfers its practice, Your records will be handled as required by PHIPA and the professional rules that apply to the transfer of health records.</p>
			<h4>Law Enforcement and Other Legal Requirements</h4>
			<p>Casa Medica may disclose Your Personal Data if required or permitted to do so by law, for example in response to a court order or valid request from a regulator or other public authority. We may also disclose it where necessary to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Comply with a legal obligation</li>
				<li>Eliminate or reduce a significant risk of serious bodily harm to a person or the public</li>
				<li>Respond to a complaint or investigation by the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Ontario or a professional regulatory body</li>
				<li>Establish, exercise or defend legal claims</li>
			</ul>
			<h3>Security of Your Personal Data</h3>
			<p>The security of Your Personal Data is important to Us. We use reasonable administrative, technical and physical safeguards to protect it, including encryption, restricted and authenticated access for Clinicians, secure sessions, and audit records. However, no method of transmission over the Internet, or method of electronic storage, is 100% secure, and We cannot guarantee absolute security.</p>
			<h3>Privacy Breaches</h3>
			<p>If Your personal health information is lost, stolen or accessed or disclosed without authorization, We will notify You as required by PHIPA, and We will report the breach to the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Ontario where required.</p>
			<h2>Children's and Minors' Privacy</h2>
			<p>The Service is intended for use by Clinicians and adult Patients. If an Examination is needed for a person who is under 18 or who is not capable of consenting, Casa Medica will involve the appropriate parent, guardian or substitute decision-maker, as required by law.</p>
			<p>If You believe that information about a child has been entered into the Service without proper authority, please contact Us and We will review the matter promptly.</p>
			<h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
			<p>The Service does not intentionally link to third-party websites. If a link to another website appears, You will be directed to that third party's site when You click it. We have no control over and assume no responsibility for the content, privacy policies or practices of any third-party sites or services, and We advise You to review the privacy policy of every site You visit.</p>
			<h2>Changes to this Privacy Policy</h2>
			<p>We may update Our Privacy Policy from time to time. We will post the new Privacy Policy on this page and update the &quot;Last updated&quot; date at the top.</p>
			<p>You are advised to review this Privacy Policy periodically for any changes. Changes to this Privacy Policy are effective when they are posted on this page.</p>
			<h2>Questions, Requests and Complaints</h2>
			<p>If You have any questions about this Privacy Policy, want to make an access or correction request, or have a concern about how Your information is handled, You can contact Casa Medica:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>By email: casamedica.clinic@gmail.com</li>
				<li>By mail: Casa Medica, 140 Woodbridge Ave. Unit 17 Second Floor L4L 4K9</li>
			</ul>
			<p>You also have the right to make a complaint to the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Ontario if You believe Your privacy rights have not been respected. You can contact the Commissioner at <a href="https://www.ipc.on.ca" target="_blank">www.ipc.on.ca</a> or by telephone at 1-800-387-0073.</p>
		</main>
	}
}

templ Terms(site config.Site) {
	@layouts.Base(site) {
		<main class="flex flex-col justify-center items-center w-full p-2 text-primary text-center legal">
			<h1>Terms and Conditions</h1>
			<p>Last updated: November 11, 2026</p>
			<p>Please read these terms and conditions carefully before using Casa Medica Examinations.</p>
			<h2>Interpretation and Definitions</h2>
			<h3>Interpretation</h3>
			<p>The words whose initial letters are capitalized have meanings defined under the following conditions. The following definitions shall have the same meaning regardless of whether they appear in singular or in plural.</p>
			<h3>Definitions</h3>
			<p>For the purposes of these Terms and Conditions:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Clinician</strong> means an authorized healthcare professional or staff member of Casa Medica who uses the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Company</strong> (referred to as either &quot;the Company&quot;, &quot;Casa Medica&quot;, &quot;We&quot;, &quot;Us&quot; or &quot;Our&quot; in these Terms and Conditions) refers to Casa Medica, 140 Woodbridge Ave. Unit 17 Second Floor L4L 4K9.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Country/State</strong> refers to: Ontario, Canada</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Device</strong> means any device that can access the Service such as a computer, a cell phone or a digital tablet.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Examination</strong> means a test, questionnaire or assessment administered to a Patient through the Service, either remotely through an Examination Link or in person at the clinic.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Examination Link</strong> means a unique link sent by email to a Patient that gives access to a specific Examination.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Patient</strong> means an individual who takes, or is asked to take, an Examination through the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Service</strong> refers to Casa Medica Examinations and the Website.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Terms and Conditions</strong> (also referred to as &quot;Terms&quot;) means these Terms and Conditions, including any documents expressly incorporated by reference, which govern Your access to and use of the Service.</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>Website</strong> refers to Casa Medica Examinations, accessible from <a href="https://casaintake.urx.ink" target="_blank">casaintake.urx.ink</a></p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<p><strong>You</strong> means the individual accessing or using the Service, as applicable.</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>Acknowledgment</h2>
			<p>These are the Terms and Conditions governing the use of this Service and the agreement between You and the Company. These Terms and Conditions set out the rights and obligations of all users regarding the use of the Service.</p>
			<p>Your access to and use of the Service is conditioned on Your acceptance of and compliance with these Terms and Conditions. These Terms and Conditions apply to all Clinicians, Patients and others who access or use the Service.</p>
			<p>By accessing or using the Service You agree to be bound by these Terms and Conditions. If You disagree with any part of these Terms and Conditions then You may not access the Service.</p>
			<p>The Service is intended for Clinicians and adult Patients. If an Examination is needed for a person who is under 18 or who is not capable of consenting, it will be arranged through Casa Medica with the involvement of the appropriate parent, guardian or substitute decision-maker.</p>
			<p>Your access to and use of the Service is also subject to Our Privacy Policy, which describes how We collect, use, and disclose personal information, including personal health information. Please read Our Privacy Policy carefully before using Our Service.</p>
			<h2>Purpose of the Service and Medical Disclaimer</h2>
			<p>Casa Medica Examinations is a tool used by Casa Medica Clinicians to administer Examinations to Patients and to record their responses and results. The Service does not provide medical advice, diagnosis or treatment.</p>
			<p>Examination results must be reviewed and interpreted by a qualified Clinician. Completing an Examination does not create a diagnosis or replace a consultation with a healthcare professional.</p>
			<p><strong>The Service is not for emergencies.</strong> The Service is not monitored in real time, and Examination responses are not reviewed immediately. If You are in crisis, are thinking about harming yourself or others, or believe You are experiencing a medical emergency, call 911 or go to the nearest emergency department. In Canada, You can also call or text 9-8-8 to reach the Suicide Crisis Helpline at any time.</p>
			<h2>Use of the Service by Clinicians</h2>
			<p>If You are a Clinician, You agree to:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Use the Service only for authorized clinical and administrative purposes of Casa Medica</li>
				<li>Keep Your login credentials confidential and not share them with anyone</li>
				<li>Enter accurate Patient information and send Examination Links only to the email address of the intended Patient</li>
				<li>Sign out of the Service when You leave a Device, especially a shared or in-clinic Device, so that Patients and others cannot see other Patients' information</li>
				<li>Access Patient information only where You have a legitimate need to do so, and comply with the Privacy Policy and all privacy laws that apply to You, including PHIPA</li>
				<li>Report any suspected unauthorized access or privacy breach to Casa Medica immediately</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>Use of Examination Links by Patients</h2>
			<p>If You are a Patient, You agree that:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>Your Examination Link is personal to You. You will not share it, forward it, or allow anyone else to complete the Examination for You.</li>
				<li>You will answer questions as honestly and completely as You can. If You have questions or concerns about an Examination, You should speak with Your Clinician.</li>
				<li>If You think Your Examination Link was received in error or has been accessed by someone else, You will contact Casa Medica as soon as possible.</li>
				<li>You may choose to complete an Examination in person at the clinic instead of through an Examination Link by letting Your Clinician know.</li>
			</ul>
			<h2>Links to Other Websites</h2>
			<p>Our Service does not intentionally link to third-party websites. If a link to a third-party website or service appears, it is not owned or controlled by the Company.</p>
			<p>The Company has no control over, and assumes no responsibility for, the content, privacy policies, or practices of any third-party websites or services. We strongly advise You to read the terms and conditions and privacy policies of any third-party websites or services that You visit.</p>
			<h2>Termination</h2>
			<p>We may terminate or suspend Your access immediately, without prior notice or liability, for any reason, including if You breach these Terms and Conditions or if We suspect unauthorized or inappropriate use of the Service.</p>
			<p>Upon termination, Your right to use the Service will cease immediately. Termination does not affect Our obligations regarding records already created, which will continue to be handled in accordance with the Privacy Policy and applicable law.</p>
			<h2>Limitation of Liability</h2>
			<p>To the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, in no event shall the Company or its suppliers be liable for any special, incidental, indirect, or consequential damages whatsoever (including, but not limited to, damages for loss of profits, loss of data or other information, or business interruption) arising out of or in any way related to the use of or inability to use the Service, third-party software and/or third-party hardware used with the Service, or otherwise in connection with any provision of these Terms, even if the Company or any supplier has been advised of the possibility of such damages.</p>
			<p>Nothing in these Terms limits any right You have under PHIPA or other applicable privacy or health legislation, or any liability that cannot be excluded or limited by law. Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of certain warranties or the limitation of liability for certain damages, which means that some of the above limitations may not apply to You. In such a case, liability will be limited to the greatest extent permitted by law.</p>
			<h2>&quot;AS IS&quot; and &quot;AS AVAILABLE&quot; Disclaimer</h2>
			<p>To the maximum extent permitted under applicable law, the Service is provided to You &quot;AS IS&quot; and &quot;AS AVAILABLE&quot; and with all faults and defects without warranty of any kind. The Company expressly disclaims all warranties, whether express, implied, statutory or otherwise, with respect to the Service, including all implied warranties of merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, title and non-infringement, and warranties that may arise out of course of dealing, course of performance, usage or trade practice.</p>
			<p>Without limiting the foregoing, the Company does not warrant that the Service will be uninterrupted or error-free, that any errors or defects will be corrected, that the Service will be available at any particular time, or that the Service, its servers, or emails sent from or on behalf of the Company are free of viruses or other harmful components. Examination content and scoring are provided for use by qualified Clinicians and must be interpreted by them in the context of each Patient.</p>
			<p>Some jurisdictions do not allow the exclusion of certain types of warranties or limitations on applicable statutory rights of a consumer, so some or all of the above exclusions and limitations may not apply to You. In such a case, the exclusions and limitations set forth in this section shall be applied to the greatest extent enforceable under applicable law.</p>
			<h2>Governing Law</h2>
			<p>The laws of the Province of Ontario and the federal laws of Canada applicable therein, excluding conflicts of law rules, shall govern these Terms and Your use of the Service.</p>
			<h2>Disputes Resolution</h2>
			<p>If You have any concern or dispute about the Service, You agree to first try to resolve the dispute informally by contacting the Company. This does not limit Your right to make a complaint to the Information and Privacy Commissioner of Ontario or to any other regulator or authority.</p>
			<h2>Severability and Waiver</h2>
			<h3>Severability</h3>
			<p>If any provision of these Terms is held to be unenforceable or invalid, such provision will be changed and interpreted to accomplish the objectives of such provision to the greatest extent possible under applicable law and the remaining provisions will continue in full force and effect.</p>
			<h3>Waiver</h3>
			<p>Except as provided herein, the failure to exercise a right or to require performance of an obligation under these Terms shall not affect a party's ability to exercise such right or require such performance at any time thereafter nor shall the waiver of a breach constitute a waiver of any subsequent breach.</p>
			<h2>Changes to These Terms and Conditions</h2>
			<p>We reserve the right to modify or replace these Terms at any time. If a revision is material We will make reasonable efforts to provide notice prior to any new terms taking effect. What constitutes a material change will be determined at Our sole discretion.</p>
			<p>By continuing to access or use Our Service after those revisions become effective, You agree to be bound by the revised terms. If You do not agree to the new terms, in whole or in part, please stop using the Service.</p>
			<h2>Contact Us</h2>
			<p>If you have any questions about these Terms and Conditions, You can contact us:</p>
			<ul>
				<li>By email: casamedica.clinic@gmail.com</li>
				<li>By mail: Casa Medica, 140 Woodbridge Ave. Unit 17 Second Floor L4L 4K9</li>
			</ul>
		</main>
	}
}
